{{!
    @template local_rangeos/empty_state

    What stands where a list's rows would be when there are none.

    An empty area is not news, so it is not an alert: it states the case quietly and, where
    there is an obvious next step, offers it. The headline says what is missing, the line
    under it says why or what to do, and the action - a link, or a button the page's own
    JavaScript picks up - is the thing the reader came to do.

    Build the context with \local_rangeos\output\empty_state so the pages stay in step.

    Context variables required:
    * title - the headline: what is missing
    * message - one line on why, or what to do about it

    Optional:
    * actionlabel - label for the action; required by either action form below
    * actionurl - render the action as a link to this URL
    * actiondata - render the action as a button with this data-action value instead

    Example context (json):
    {
        "title": "No environments yet",
        "message": "Add a RangeOS environment to connect this site to a range.",
        "actionlabel": "Add environment",
        "actionurl": "/local/rangeos/environment_profiles.php?action=add"
    }
}}
<div class="rangeos-empty-state">
    <span class="rangeos-empty-state-icon" aria-hidden="true">
        {{! A tray: the shape of a list with nothing in it. }}
        <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" focusable="false"><path d="M3 15h4l1.5 2.5h7L17 15h4"/><path d="M4.5 15 6 5.5h12L19.5 15"/></svg>
    </span>
    <p class="rangeos-empty-state-title">{{title}}</p>
    <p class="rangeos-empty-state-message">{{message}}</p>
    {{#actionlabel}}
    {{#actionurl}}
    <a href="{{actionurl}}" class="btn btn-primary">{{actionlabel}}</a>
    {{/actionurl}}
    {{#actiondata}}
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-action="{{actiondata}}">{{actionlabel}}</button>
    {{/actiondata}}
    {{/actionlabel}}
</div>
